data · tier 1 · 52 of 59 functions in this release

  frame             Create a frame from named lists of values
  import            Read a data file into a frame
  n_rows            Number of rows
  n_cols            Number of variables
  variables         List of variable names
  head              First n rows
  tail              Last n rows
  where             Keep the rows where a condition is true
  select            Keep only the named variables
  drop              Remove the named variables
  rename            Rename variables; the new name is on the left
  add               Add variables computed from the frame
  update            Change the values of a variable, everywhere or where a condition holds
  label             Set a variable's label, or the labels its codes stand for
  recode            Map a variable's values, merge a category's levels, or move labelled codes
  panel             Declare unit and time variables
  sort              Sort rows; stable, NA last
  describe          Type, non-missing and missing count of each variable
  mean              Mean of a variable
  sd                Sample standard deviation
  variance          Sample variance (n − 1)
  median            Median
  quantile          Sample quantiles
  min               Smallest non-missing value
  max               Largest non-missing value
  sum               Compensated sum of non-missing values
  n                 Row count, as a reducer inside add and aggregate
  n_distinct        Number of distinct values
  summary           Table of N, missing, mean, SD, min and max
  drop_missing      Remove rows with NA in the variables and report how many
  lag               Previous values in the panel's time order
  lead              Next values
  diff              x − lag(x, n), so it respects the panel's time order and gaps
  fill_forward      Replace NA with the last non-missing value, within panel units or by: groups
  running_sum       Cumulative sum down the rows; an NA makes the rest NA
  running_product   Cumulative product down the rows; an NA makes the rest NA
  rank              Rank of each value, smallest first; NA stays NA
  bin               Category from numeric intervals, (a, b] by default as in R
  quantile_group    Group 1 to n by cutting at sample quantiles; tied values share a group
  distinct          Rows with distinct values of the variables, the first occurrence kept
  duplicates        Table of repeated key values
  sample            Random sample of rows; the seed is recorded
  row_mean          Mean across variables in each row
  row_sum           Sum across variables in each row
  between           True where low <= x <= high
  center            Subtract the mean
  standardize       z-scores
  iqr               Interquartile range
  mad               Median absolute deviation
  skewness          Sample skewness
  kurtosis          Sample kurtosis
  winsorize         Cap values below the at quantile and above the 1 − at quantile

the rest arrive with later releases; `zeff help <name>` says when
